<article> <header class="hero"> <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"> <a href="/">Home</a> <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg> <a href="/glossary">Glossary</a> <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><polyline points="9 18 15 12 9 6"/></svg> <span>CUTOVER2026 keyword</span> </nav> <div class="hero-badge"><span class="pulse-dot"></span><span style="position:relative;z-index:1">Glossary · Schemes & Rules</span></div> <h1><span class="accent">CUTOVER2026 keyword</span></h1> <p class="page-meta">Glossary entry · Last reviewed 26 July 2026</p> <!-- ANSWER BLOCK — picked up by speakable schema --> <p class="answer-block"><strong>CUTOVER2026</strong> is a literal keyword placed in <code>&lt;TwnNm&gt;</code> as a last-resort bridge for return messages and warehoused payments that straddle the <strong>15 November 2026</strong> cutover. Prohibited in newly initiated payments (PMPG Hybrid Postal Address v1.12 §0.311), it expires approximately three months post-cutover, after which Best-Effort Structuring is the only permitted handling.</p> </header> <section class="section"> <div class="section-label">In Practice</div> <h2 class="section-title">How CUTOVER2026 keyword works in practice</h2> <div class="content-block"><p>The keyword is Tier 2 of the transitional regime: institutions must first attempt Best-Effort Structuring (§38) and may fall back to CUTOVER2026 (§39) only where <code>&lt;TwnNm&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;Ctry&gt;</code> cannot be reliably derived. Where <code>&lt;Ctry&gt;</code> is taken from the Creditor Agent BIC, a documented risk acknowledgment is mandatory (§40.1). It must never become standard market practice.</p></div> <p class="src">Source: PMPG Hybrid Postal Address v1.12 §7 / §39–§40, p42–45 (§0.310–§0.311 / p43); the ioNova Postal Address Specification v2.0 PART XIII, Appendix I Q3–Q5.</p> <div class="content-block"><p>The bridging form — in-flight transactions only:</p></div>
<div class="code-block"><pre><span class="cmt">&lt;!-- Last-resort bridge — in-flight transactions only --&gt;</span>
<span class="tag">&lt;PstlAdr&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;TwnNm&gt;</span>CUTOVER2026<span class="tag">&lt;/TwnNm&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;Ctry&gt;</span>NZ<span class="tag">&lt;/Ctry&gt;</span>  <span class="cmt">&lt;!-- derived from Creditor Agent BIC, last resort --&gt;</span>
  <span class="tag">&lt;AdrLine&gt;</span>169 CUBA STREET, WELLINGTON 6011, NEW ZEALAND<span class="tag">&lt;/AdrLine&gt;</span>
<span class="tag">&lt;/PstlAdr&gt;</span></pre></div> <div class="content-block"><p>Parent reference: <a href="/address-intelligence/structured-address-mandate">ISO 20022 deadline — the structured address mandate</a>.</p></div> </section> <section class="section"> <div class="section-label">Citations</div> <h2 class="section-title">Sources</h2> <div class="sources-list"> <h3 class="sources-subhead">Standards &amp; regulatory sources</h3>
